  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "MqttClient_HandlePacket",
    "file": "wolfmqtt/src/mqtt_client.c",
    "description": "In the PUBLISH handling path, `MqttClient_HandlePacket` unconditionally calls `MqttProps_Free(publish->props)` for MQTT v5 after payload processing, but `publish->props` can contain an invalid/untrusted pointer value produced by packet decoding/state reuse. `MqttProps_Free` then walks that pointer as a linked list and writes `head->type = MQTT_PROP_NONE` (mqtt_packet.c:1902), causing a write to an attacker-controlled invalid address and SEGV.",
    "conditions": "During `MqttClient_Subscribe` -> `MqttClient_WaitType`, the fuzzer supplies malformed incoming packet bytes that are treated as inbound packets (including publish-related state). Under MQTT v5 build, when `MqttClient_HandlePacket` reaches the PUBLISH cleanup path, `publish->props` is not validated/initialized to a safe list head before free. If crafted input leaves `publish->props` as a bogus non-NULL pointer, `MqttProps_Free` dereferences and writes through it, crashing."
  },
